From b79fe0a73b43bf4b7cd563147f5742721c59616d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tron <tron@tsmconsultz.com>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 02:55:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] feat(mortgage): add Business Impact Delta to strategist
 page

Adds a No-Action / With-Action exposure projection using the shared
TSMBNCAExposureEngine (same engine as Insurance/RE/Healthcare/BPO/
FinOps/Legal/HotelOps). Base exposure reuses financials.total_exposure
-- a figure mortgage-engine.js already computes deterministically from
the financial_model rate card (closing_delay_cost_per_day x SLA-breach
hours, plus compliance_exposure_by_severity x open exceptions) and
already includes in the relay payload; the strategist page just wasn't
reading it. Severity is banded from the loans-over-SLA ratio using the
same thresholds the war room's own mtgBreachSeverity() uses.

Honesty pattern: if total_exposure is 0 -- which the engine itself
documents can mean either 'no risk' or 'rate card incomplete' -- shows
the engine's own financial_model.note (when present) instead of a
misleadingly clean /bin/sh delta.
